# SNIP architecture (this repository)

This repo is the first **SNIP domain application** (Network Planning & Optimisation), not the entire Simba Network Intelligence Platform.

Read before changing code:

- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-CONTEXT.md` (section 0 is authoritative for scope)
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-STATUS.md`
- `docs/architecture/SNIP-PHASE-3-ASSURANCE-DECISION-INTELLIGENCE-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-PHASE-3-ASSURANCE-DECISION-INTELLIGENCE-SPECIFICATION.md`

Root copies of the Phase 3 documents also exist:

- `SNIP-PHASE-3-ASSURANCE-DECISION-INTELLIGENCE-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `SNIP-PHASE-3-ASSURANCE-DECISION-INTELLIGENCE-SPECIFICATION.md`

## Authorised now

Phase **3** is architecturally accepted and **frozen** on the Phase 2 baseline (`8c70537bec048f2bf7e55c0ca626c8deec7b8670`). Do not add Phase 3 functionality, resolve deferred technical debt, or refactor for its own sake.

Preserve Phase 1A/1A.1/1B/2/3. Kafka remains off by default. Do not vectorize operational telemetry or Assurance Case state. Phase 3 is read-only for the network. Detection is deterministic. The LLM explains and prioritises investigation; it does not decide thresholds, severity, or confidence. Automatic resolution remains deferred; evidence on the active case remains a replaced snapshot; duplicate telemetry event IDs skip detection; retrieval may expand with deterministically established `caseType` and semantic descriptors only.

## Do not implement

MCP, Agent Factory, autonomous agents, live OSS/NMS/EMS integrations, live gNB/network writes, incident-management / ITSM, Schema Registry, Avro, Protobuf, Flink, Spark, Kafka Streams, dedicated time-series DB, EKS/Kubernetes, Kong, ALB, ALICE, RL, ML anomaly detection, adaptive thresholds, forecasting, billing, Ionic, AWS lock-in, Phase 4.

## Rules

- Extend Phase 1A/1B/2 abstractions. Do not rewrite the slice.
- Keep recommendations, domain, and assurance APIs read-only. No apply/execute/write-to-network APIs.
- If retrieval is empty, do not fabricate citations.
- Ordinary CI must not download large models. PostgreSQL via Testcontainers remains required. Kafka Testcontainers remains allowed.
- Implementation markdown lives under `docs/implementation/`. ADRs under `docs/architecture/adr/`.
- Architecture document has architectural authority. Implementation specification is the authorised execution scope.
